              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioner Mr. Pereida argued that because it is unclear whether his crime involved moral turpitude, he should remain eligible for immigration relief."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e06fa515ec7e0ff0900f3ed7946fb40af5a67134ae5eae6b34b664120cfb0222",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e06fa515ec7e-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Counsel asked the immigration judge to postpone further proceedings on Mr. Pereida\u2019s relief application until his criminal case concluded, and the judge agreed."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Background and Question",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "case_id": "2020-19-438",
  "decision": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e06fa515ec7e0ff0900f3ed7946fb40af5a67134ae5eae6b34b664120cfb0222",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e06fa515ec7e-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 9,
              "start": 9
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The majority held that any lingering uncertainty about whether Mr. Pereida was convicted of a crime involving moral turpitude defeats his application for relief."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e06fa515ec7e0ff0900f3ed7946fb40af5a67134ae5eae6b34b664120cfb0222",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e06fa515ec7e-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 30,
              "start": 30
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer (dissent) stated there is no unresolved factual question because the conviction is undisputed, and that unless the offense is necessarily a crime involving moral turpitude, the judge must find it is not."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e06fa515ec7e0ff0900f3ed7946fb40af5a67134ae5eae6b34b664120cfb0222",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e06fa515ec7e-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 33,
              "start": 33
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer (dissent) also argued that the petitioner should not bear the burden of proof because the evidence sought lies beyond the limited record allowed by precedent."
      }
    ],
